      ],
      "source": "https://www.cheatlake.com/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Cheat Lake was first officially named Lake Lynn, but locals unofficially called it Cheat Lake until the government changed it back.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cheatlake.com/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A bustling keg and nail factory once operated on the shores of the Cheat River, floating its products downstream.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cheatlake.com/history"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "An official dedication ceremony for Cheat Lake took place on September 14, 1927, featuring a bronze tablet near the power station.",
